description:
Aypa Power is a leading developer, owner, and operator of utility-scale energy storage and hybrid renewable projects that power our communities and cities. Our mission is to responsibly decarbonize the grid and make North American energy markets more affordable, sustainable, and efficient. Aypa is well-capitalized and uniquely positioned to lean forward on projects with well-suited deal structures to meet our customers' needs. We have been at the forefront of energy storage development since our first energy storage project came online in 2018. As a leader in our industry, we have over 22 GW of utility-scale energy storage and hybrid renewable energy projects in development and 33 projects in operation or construction across North America.

The Director, Pre-Construction will play a critical role in the development and execution of Aypa's portfolio of stand-alone battery storage and hybrid projects. This role will work closely with internal and external stakeholders to successfully plan, design, and prepare projects during the pre-construction phase.

**Responsibilities:**

* Lead, mentor, and develop a team of two (2) to three (3) direct reports, delegating workstreams effectively, setting clear priorities, and holding the team accountable for quality and deadlines;
* Develop and own integrated project execution schedules for utility-scale BESS and hybrid projects, identifying the critical path across engineering, major equipment lead times, permitting, interconnection, construction, and commissioning through COD; support the formation of project budgets;
* Collaborate with management to identify and review project risks, develop mitigation strategies, and ensure all potential issues are addressed proactively;
* Coordinate and contribute to engineering design reviews during late-stage development and provide input regarding feasibility and constructability;
